@* The component router.

   It deliberately declares no @rendermode, so anything it reaches is statically
   server-rendered.

   The review screen is NOT reached through this router. `ReviewEndpoints` returns
   `RazorComponentResult<ReviewPage>` from a minimal endpoint that has already
   authenticated the caller, revalidated the membership, and resolved the trusted
   firm. Routing a taxpayer page here instead would move the safe-404 and
   authorization decisions into component discovery, and a refused request could
   render a partial page before the refusal was reached. `ReviewPage` therefore
   carries no @page directive at all.

   `AppAssembly` is this assembly, so no other assembly can contribute a route. *@

<Router AppAssembly="@typeof(Routes).Assembly">
    <Found Context="routeData">
        <RouteView RouteData="@routeData" DefaultLayout="@typeof(PortalLayout)" />
    </Found>
</Router>
